layout: base.njk
title: "Glossary"
description: "Definitions of the DPRK campaign, malware and vendor naming terms used across the site, each with its source, and of every label on its badges."
permalink: "/glossary/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
  src/glossary/index.njk — Glossary

  One entry per record in src/_data/glossary.json, rendered in the file's
  order. Records with no `group` are the vocabulary of the reporting itself
  (organisational terms, campaigns, malware, laundering); each definition is
  written from its cited source and links to it, and an entry with a `see`
  field also links to the page on this site where the term is used.

  Records with a `group` define the labels this site puts on its own badges,
  under "Labels used on this site". They carry an explicit `id` rather than a
  slug of the term, because badges elsewhere link to those anchors and a
  reworded term must not move one. They have no external `source`: what they
  define is this site's own vocabulary, and the `see` link names the page that
  shows it. `labelGroups` below sets the order and headings of the groups; a
  record whose group is not listed there does not render.
#}
{% set labelGroups = [
  { key: "confidence", id: "labels-confidence", title: "Confidence levels", intro: "A confidence badge means something slightly different depending on what it is attached to. On a named individual's profile it is the cited source's characterisation; elsewhere it is set out below." },
  { key: "provenance", id: "labels-provenance", title: "Provenance labels", intro: "Every indicator carries one label saying how the value reached the index. Where several sources hold the same value, the label comes from the first route in this order: the hand-curated ruleset and watchlist; researchers' posts, registries and the site's own observations; scraped reports; bulk lists; and candidates under review. Every source is still cited." },
  { key: "status", id: "labels-status", title: "Status labels", intro: "A status records the result of a check made on a stated date, shown beside it. It is true as of that date only. Accounts are deleted and re-registered, packages are pulled and republished, and addresses change hands, so every status goes stale from the day it is taken." },
  { key: "other", id: "labels-other", title: "Other labels", intro: "" }
] %}
<section>
  <h1>Glossary</h1>
  <p>
    Reporting on DPRK cyber operations uses several overlapping vocabularies
    at once: the names vendors assign to clusters, the names campaigns and
    malware families acquire, and the organisational terms from government
    records. This page defines the ones that appear across this site. Each
    definition is drawn from the cited source, and the
    <a href="/#actor-cluster-taxonomy">cluster pages</a> carry the full alias
    list for each actor. The <a href="#labels">labels</a> this site puts on its
    badges are defined at the end.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <ul class="reading-list">
    {% for entry in glossary %}{% if not entry.group %}
    <li id="{{ entry.term | slugify }}">
      <h2 class="glossary__term">{{ entry.term }}</h2>
      <p>{{ entry.definition }}</p>
      <span class="reading-list__meta">
        Source:
        {% set externalLink = { url: entry.source.url, text: entry.source.title } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}
        &middot; {{ entry.source.publisher }}{% if entry.source.date %} &middot; {{ entry.source.date }}{% endif %}
        {%- if entry.see %} &middot; <a href="{{ entry.see.url }}">{{ entry.see.label }}</a>{% endif %}
      </span>
    </li>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="labels">Labels used on this site</h2>
  <p>
    What each badge on the site means, what was checked to set it, and where
    it appears.
  </p>
  {% for group in labelGroups %}
  <h3 id="{{ group.id }}">{{ group.title }}</h3>
  {% if group.intro %}<p>{{ group.intro }}</p>{% endif %}
  <ul class="reading-list">
    {% for entry in glossary %}{% if entry.group == group.key %}
    <li id="{{ entry.id }}">
      <h4 class="glossary__term">{{ entry.term }}</h4>
      <p>{{ entry.definition }}</p>
      {% if entry.see %}<span class="reading-list__meta">See <a href="{{ entry.see.url }}">{{ entry.see.label }}</a></span>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
